tion and type 2 diabetes. This gene may also play a role in tumor development and progression. Alternatively spliced transcript variants encoding multiple isoforms have been observed for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Jan 2014].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P16519","text":"Serine endopeptidase which is involved in the processing of hormone and other protein precursors at sites comprised of pairs of basic amino acid residues (PubMed:28719828, PubMed:7626024, PubMed:8879041, PubMed:9287128). Responsible for the release of glucagon from proglucagon in pancreatic A cells (PubMed:9287128). Mediates the release of insulin from proinsulin (PubMed:7626024)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}